=[ Install Tomet and Sisho ]

This page describes how to install the Tomet language tools and editor integrations.

==[ What you need ]

You need two command-line tools:

- `tomet`: the language tool that parses, checks, formats, and exports Tomet documents.
- `sisho`: an orchestrator that runs `tomet`, `twrit`, and `catasto` through one interface.

`sisho` does not install the other tools; it finds them on your `PATH`.
`sisho` requires `tomet` 0.5.0, `twrit` 0.2.0, and `catasto` 0.1.0.

==[ Quick install ]#(quick-install)

The quickest way to get `sisho` and `tomet` together is with Nix:

```bash
`` nix profile install github:tomet-lang/sisho#toolchain
```

The `toolchain` package bundles `sisho`, `tomet`, `twrit`, `catasto`, and `sisho-desk`.

==[ Command-line tools ]

===[ Nix ]#(nix)

Nix provides reproducible packages for Linux and macOS.

Install `tomet` and `sisho` from their flakes:

```bash
`` nix profile install github:tomet-lang/tomet#tomet
`` nix profile install github:tomet-lang/sisho#sisho
```

Binary cache: `tomet.cachix.org`. Add `https://tomet.cachix.org` to `substituters` and `tomet.cachix.org-1:9c/iO8Tb6YOM+3r55t12W3fOJK+66itPEaIe8Rs9MDw=` to `trusted-public-keys`.

===[ Build from source ]

Building from source requires a Rust toolchain (Rust 1.85 or later and Cargo).

Build the `tomet` binary from this repository:

```bash
`` cargo build --release -p tomet-cli
```

This places the executable `tomet` in `target/release/tomet`.

Build `sisho` from its repository:

```bash
`` git clone https://github.com/tomet-lang/sisho.git
`` cd sisho
`` cargo build --release -p sisho-cli
```

This places the executable `sisho` in `target/release/sisho`. Move both executables to a directory on your `PATH`.

===[ Release binaries ]

@callout(warning)
| Not available yet.

Pre-built binaries for Linux, macOS, and Windows are available on GitHub Releases:

- https://github.com/tomet-lang/tomet/releases
- https://github.com/tomet-lang/sisho/releases

Download the archive for your operating system and architecture, unpack it, and place the executable on your `PATH`.

===[ Homebrew ]

@callout(warning)
| Not available yet.

Install `tomet` and `sisho` using Homebrew:

```bash
`` brew install tomet-lang/tap/tomet tomet-lang/tap/sisho
```

This installs both tools from the `tomet-lang/homebrew-tap` tap.

===[ cargo install ]

@callout(warning)
| Not available yet.

Install the tools from crates.io with Cargo:

```bash
`` cargo install tomet-cli --locked
`` cargo install sisho-cli --locked
```

The `tomet-cli` package installs the `tomet` executable. The `sisho-cli` package installs the `sisho` executable.

==[ Editors ]#(editors)

Install an editor extension for syntax highlighting and language server integration.

===[ VS Code ]

Install the official extension from the Visual Studio Marketplace:

```bash
`` code --install-extension tomet-lang.tomet
```

===[ Open VSX ]

@callout(warning)
| Not available yet.

For VSCodium and other editors that use the Open VSX Registry:

```bash
`` codium --install-extension tomet-lang.tomet
```

===[ Zed ]

@callout(warning)
| Not available yet.

The extension source is in the @dir(editors/zed/) directory. It is not yet available in the Zed extension registry.

===[ Helix and Neovim ]

Both Helix and Neovim support Tomet through Tree-sitter and the language server.
Follow the setup instructions in @file(editors/helix/README.md) for Helix and @file(editors/neovim/README.md) for Neovim.

===[ Language server ]

The language server `tomet-lsp` provides diagnostics, syntax navigation, and hover documentation.
It is packaged with Nix:

```bash
`` nix profile install github:tomet-lang/sisho#tomet-lsp
```

==[ From code (libraries) ]

===[ npm ]

The `@tomet/wasm` package provides WebAssembly bindings for JavaScript and TypeScript:

```bash
`` npm install @tomet/wasm
```

Initialize the WebAssembly module, then convert or format Tomet markup:

```javascript
`` import init, { toHtml } from "@tomet/wasm";
``
`` await init();
`` const html = toHtml("=[ Hello ]");
```

===[ Rust ]

@callout(warning)
| Not available yet.

Add `tomet` to your `Cargo.toml`:

```toml
`` [dependencies]
`` tomet = "0.5"
```

===[ Python ]

@callout(warning)
| Not available yet.

Install the Python package from PyPI:

```bash
`` pip install tomet
```

